    summary: 'A planning-only 6.4-mile Rondout Creek whitewater reach from the High Falls Dam access area to the Rosendale/Wallkill River finish. American Whitewater rates the named section Class II–IV with possible V/V+ features, including an approximately 12-foot Little Falls, a low-head dam, strong eddy lines, holes, and the Eye Ripper. Riverfacts supplies the mapped endpoint anchors; the direct Rosendale gauge is context, not a go signal, and every feature and landing requires same-day inspection.',
