      'This route is not a casual flatwater loop. Wear a fitted PFD and cold-water protection, carry a throwline, spare paddle, repair kit, communication plan, and footwear for repeated legal carries around wood and beaver obstructions.',
      'Spring rain and snowmelt can raise the kill quickly. Compare the direct Coons gauge with recent rainfall and visual water level, and turn around when strainers, fences, unstable banks, or a blocked channel remove rescue margin.',
      'American Whitewater rates the Tenandeho section Class II, but narrow rocky chutes and changing wood can create higher consequences. Scout from legal shore, never run blind ledges or strainers, and do not confuse the race route with a safety certification.',
      'Use only the Round Lake Preserve and Mechanicville City Dock access areas. Respect private banks, agricultural fields, bridges, construction, and posted hours; take out at the dock before entering the broader Hudson or approaching dam infrastructure.',
