      'The downstream take-out is at the mouth of Irondequoit Creek. Check wind, waves, wakes, motorboat traffic, and visibility before entering the bay or landing; a calm creek reading does not make the open bay safe.',
      'Keep a fitted PFD on, carry a whistle and phone in a dry case, and use a float plan. Treat muddy banks, private shorelines, road crossings, and wetland wildlife areas as no-landing zones unless the public launch or park explicitly authorizes them.',
