    summary: 'A short, flatwater Cayuga Inlet reach from the current Allan H. Treman State Marine Park boat launch to the City of Ithaca’s Cass Park human-powered launch. The state Blueway guide places the endpoints within a broader southern Cayuga Lake paddling loop, while the Tompkins County guide identifies the inlet launches and warns of crew activity. Use the 04233255 USGS station as a clearly labeled same-inlet proxy: it is upstream at a flood-control weir, not a route-local safety certification.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only flatwater route. Launch at the current Allan H. Treman State Marine Park ramp or Cass Park human-powered launch after confirming fees, parking, docks, and current access. Check USGS 04233255 as same-inlet context, but make the day-of call from wind, lake level, current, crew shells, marina traffic, weeds, water quality, and visual depth; no numeric cfs rule is asserted. Keep the route inside the inlet and turn around before entering Cayuga Lake or any restricted marina channel unless a separate plan supports it.',
