      'Allan H. Treman is an active marina and trailer launch, not a quiet hand-launch beach. Use the canoe/kayak rack or designated non-trailer entry, yield to powered and rowing traffic, and confirm current parking/carry logistics.',
      'Cass Park’s human-powered launch is public but the Tompkins County guide notes limited parking. Do not block park roads, use a private dock, or assume an event-day landing remains available.',
      'The state Blueway guide describes a broader loop involving the inlet, Six Mile Creek, the flood-control channel, and Cayuga Lake. This card intentionally stops at Cass Park and does not claim the connected loop, lake crossing, or tributary sections.',
      'The USGS station is upstream of the bounded route and can be influenced by the flood-control weir. Keep the proxy label and visual-only flow posture visible.',
