    summary: 'A long Upper Delaware access-to-access corridor from the public Hancock River Access through the Lordville and Long Eddy area to the Callicoon NY DEC access. The National Park Service publishes the free-flowing 73.4-mile river, public launch-only rule, access sequence, approximate 27-mile Hancock-to-Callicoon distance, direct Callicoon gauge relationship, and limited primitive-camping posture. This is a planning corridor for a multi-section trip, not a promise that every paddler should complete it in one day.',
