      'Wear a fitted PFD and keep it on. NPS requires everyone to wear one at 6 ft or higher at the Callicoon gauge for this upstream section and during November–April; at 8–12 ft only skilled and experienced paddlers should consider the river, and at 12 ft or higher boating is not recommended.',
      'Watch for current stronger than it appears, cold water, strainers, sweepers, submerged eel weirs, changing channels, wakes, storms, and new debris after high water. Do not swim bridge approaches or land at private homes, docks, or utility property.',
