    summary: 'A six-mile Ramapo River moving-water run from the Tuxedo DEC parking access to H. Pierson Mapes Flat Rock Park in Hillburn. American Whitewater describes beginner-friendly Class I–II water with isolated higher-consequence dams and drops, while current KCCNY programming identifies the Tuxedo DEC lot as the launch and Rockland County documents Flat Rock as the river’s best public canoe access. The Suffern gauge is retained as a same-river downstream proxy.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only moving-water route. Use USGS 01387420 at Suffern as a downstream stage and discharge proxy; a recent American Whitewater report ran the route at 2.9 ft, while low flow can become scratchy and higher flow increases dam, wood, and strainer consequences. Confirm the Tuxedo DEC lot is open for boat entry, avoid any municipal restriction on entering the Ramapo, portage every dam/low-head feature, and take out at the county Flat Rock canoe-access park.',
