    riskLevel: 'advanced',
    confidenceNotes: 'High corridor and downstream-access confidence, conditional launch confidence: American Whitewater publishes the matching Tuxedo-to-Suffern reach, access sequence, flow observations, feature hazards, and a recent 2.9-ft trip report; KCCNY identifies the active Tuxedo DEC parking launch; Rockland County documents Flat Rock canoe access; and USGS 01387420 provides live same-river telemetry downstream. The start is retained as conditional because local parking/entry restrictions can change.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'This is moving water, not flatwater. Wear a fitted PFD; use a helmet and cold-water protection when conditions warrant; paddle with a competent group; carry rescue equipment, a float plan, and reliable communications.',
      'Use 2.9 ft at USGS 01387420 only as a recent runnable reference, not a guarantee. The gauge is downstream of the route and flow is affected by upstream diversion and occasional Lake Sebago regulation; compare trend, rainfall, local visual depth, and wood conditions before departure.',
      'Portage the Augusta Furnace/Tuxedo Falls complex, Sloatsburg Dam/Ramapo Falls, the old dams, the substation dam, and any feature with recirculation, junk, or unclear landing. Never rely on a narrow sneak line or a disappearing eddy at higher water.',
      'American Whitewater and recent trip reports document numerous strainers and changing wood. Scout bridges, bends, undercuts, islands, and dam approaches from legal locations; turn around or carry when the channel is blocked.',
      'End at H. Pierson Mapes Flat Rock Park. Do not extend through the lower river or across the New Jersey boundary without a separate access, shuttle, and jurisdiction plan; do not land on private banks.',
    ],
    shuttle: 'Stage the downstream vehicle at H. Pierson Mapes Flat Rock Park, then drive to the Tuxedo DEC parking access. Confirm both parking locations and the legal carry before committing; the train station/municipal lots may have separate fee, permit, or overnight rules.',
    camping: 'No route camping is claimed. Flat Rock has no restrooms and is a day-use canoe/fishing access; use a separate, reservation-backed campground or lodging option and do not infer camping rights from county river access.',
    campingClassification: 'nearby_basecamp',
