    accessCaveats: [
      'The Tuxedo launch is supported by current organized-paddling access information and American Whitewater trip practice, but the town/DEC parking and water-entry rules must be checked at the time of travel.',
      'Rockland County calls Flat Rock the best public Ramapo access, but parking is limited and the river carry/landing is not a full-service ramp. Keep vehicles clear of the road and confirm the exact take-out point.',
      'The USGS station is downstream near Suffern and is a proxy for this upper reach. Diversion and Lake Sebago regulation can decouple the reading from local features.',
      'NYSDEC public-water access rights still require a legal initial access point. Do not use private land, bridge embankments, or a posted municipal park as an improvised launch or portage.',
    ],
