    summary: 'A short, advanced Croton River whitewater reach from below New Croton Dam to the public Echo Canoe Launch near the Croton-Harmon station. American Whitewater documents the named rapids, low-head dams, bridge/wood hazards, portage decisions, and station-specific stage guidance; the Village and Empire State Water Trail document the downstream public launch. The dam-side start remains conditional and must be confirmed locally before unloading.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only advanced whitewater. Use direct USGS 01375000 at New Croton Dam as the stage check, with approximately 3 ft as a conservative shallow-water screen around Black Rock/Rock Slide; this is not a safe upper limit. American Whitewater describes Class II–III water with Class IV consequences at named features, low-head dams, wood, and changing eddies. Do not launch from Croton Gorge Park or below the dam unless current Westchester County/park permission and a legal water entry are confirmed; portage every dam and take out at Echo before the Hudson.',
