    camping: 'NYSDEC documents designated primitive tent sites on the Hudson River that are accessible by water only, including Polaris Bridge and Cedar River sites. Use only marked designated sites, follow first-come rules and state-land regulations, and verify weather, fire, group-size, and seasonal access conditions. Nearby Lake Harris or Indian Lake campgrounds are separate basecamp options.',
