    confidenceNotes: 'Moderate corridor confidence with a conditional access posture: CanWePaddle publishes the matching thirteen-mile reach, Class I character, direct Gowanda gauge, season, and 150–3,000 cfs planning range; New York planning documents identify the Gowanda Gateway Park watercraft launch; NYS Parks and Chautauqua County identify the Sunset Bay public launch. Because the Seneca Nation identifies its Cattaraugus Territory along the downstream corridor and current paddling permission is not established by the public launch listings, this route remains conditional/planning-oriented until the Nation’s current restrictions are confirmed.',
    permits: 'Gateway Park and Sunset Bay are public launch locations, but the river corridor downstream of Gowanda intersects the Seneca Nation Cattaraugus Territory. Contact the Seneca Nation Cattaraugus office or current managing authority before launching and obtain any required permission; do not infer that a public endpoint authorizes travel through the entire corridor. Also check current NYS/Seneca water-quality advisories, launch fees, seasonal hours, and posted restrictions.',
