      'NYSDEC warns that Cattaraugus Creek whitewater and gorge conditions can range from Class 2 to Class 4 depending on water level, with strainers as a common hazard. This lower route is not the same as the North Otto gorge run, but the warning supports conservative scouting and a hard no-go when the creek is rising or debris-loaded.',
      'The Seneca Nation identifies the Cattaraugus Territory as extending along Cattaraugus Creek from Gowanda downstream to Lake Erie. Confirm current permission or restrictions before launching; do not land, camp, scout, or trespass on Nation or private banks without authorization.',
      'Check the Seneca Nation water-quality advisory and any major-rain advisory before entering the lower creek. The Sunset Bay take-out is close to Lake Erie, so wind, waves, mouth bars, cold water, and changing launch traffic can control the final take-out even when the upstream gauge is favorable.',
