    summary: 'A public-access approximately 7.7-mile one-way Erie Canal Water Trail paddle from the Brockport Welcome Center/Harvester Park to the Spencerport Village Docks. The official Canalway stewardship inventory identifies the broader Section 7 boundary as 10.7 miles from the San Souci boundary to Spencerport, with Brockport and Spencerport as the named launches; the guidebook documents Brockport’s accessible low-wall launch, Arrowhead/Adams Basin navigation context, Spencerport’s floating dock and village services, and the lift-bridge and guard-gate sequence. This remains planning-only because the reach is high traffic and USGS 04218700 is a proxy rather than a route-specific go/no-go gauge.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only one-way canal route. Launch from the documented Brockport Welcome Center/Harvester Park access, follow the marked channel east through the Adams Basin and other bridge controls, and finish at the Spencerport Village Docks west of the Union Street lift bridge. Confirm dock access, bridge operations, traffic, parking, and the shuttle before departure; do not treat the official San Souci boundary as an additional launch unless separately verified.',
