    difficultyNotes: 'The route is protected canal flatwater but includes high recreational and rowing traffic, bridge and lock controls, a steep Lock E33 portage, the Lock 32 whitewater/spillway hazard, elevated Great Embankment exposure, wakes, cold water, vertical walls, and limited legal egress.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High corridor confidence: the official Canalway stewardship inventory publishes this distinct 9.3-mile Genesee River–Bushnell’s Basin section and its public/near-water access chain. The Rochester guidebook supplies the endpoint coordinates, facilities, lock and spillway warnings, rowing and motor-boat traffic context, Great Embankment exposure, and Bushnell’s Basin finish; NYSDEC confirms Brighton, Pittsford, and Bushnell’s Basin launch listings. USGS 04218700 is a same-canal proxy and no numeric threshold is asserted.',
    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 04218700 measures the Erie Barge Canal west of the Genesee River at Rochester and is used as a same-canal proxy. Canal pool level, local weeds/debris, wind, wakes, rowing activity, lock/guard-gate operations, and launch condition can differ materially; the gauge does not authorize lock passage or entry to spillways.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'Wear a fitted PFD and carry a communication plan, spare paddle, light, and cold-water layer. Stay visible to motorized traffic, rowing crews, and tour boats; keep the group together in the marked channel.',
      'Use USGS 04218700 as proxy context only. The official section source publishes no numeric runnable band; inspect actual canal level, weeds, debris, wakes, weather, and access before launch.',
      'Portage every lock and guard-gate control unless current Canal Corporation instructions explicitly provide a safe paddler procedure. Do not enter the Lock E33 south-side spillway, Lock E32 hydraulics, lock chambers, or guard-gate machinery.',
      'Great Embankment crosses high above Irondequoit Creek and can feel exposed in wind. Bushnell’s Basin is a popular boating stop; slow down, yield, and avoid collisions and wakes near docks and bridges.',
    ],
    shuttle: 'Stage the downstream vehicle at confirmed Bushnell’s Basin Docks, then drive to the confirmed Brighton Reserve or DEC Pittsford launch. Use the East Guard Lock only as a section-boundary reference unless current public access is separately confirmed; allow extra time for lock-area portages, rowing activity, traffic, and dock congestion.',
    camping: 'Bushnell’s Basin has documented boater amenities and nearby lodging, but no campsite is claimed for this exact one-way section. Use separately verified managed lodging or campground options; do not camp at Brighton Reserve, Lock 32, Pittsford parks, Great Embankment, Bushnell’s Basin, canal banks, or private shoreline without explicit permission.',
