    confidenceNotes: 'High corridor confidence: the official Canalway stewardship inventory publishes this distinct 14.4-mile Lyons-to-Seneca County Line section and its Lauraville, Lock E26, and Armitage access chain. The Rochester-to-Syracuse guidebook supplies the coordinates, Clyde channel guidance, vegetation/debris warning, Lock E26 movable-dam exclusion, Lauraville facilities and free-permit camping, and Armitage informal bank-launch context. USGS 04237496 is a broad Seneca River proxy and no numeric threshold is asserted.',
    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 04237496 is on the Seneca River near Baldwinsville, west of this eastern Clyde/Erie reach, and is used only as broad watershed and flood-trend context. Local canal pool levels, wind, vegetation, debris, Clyde backwater, Lock E26 controls, refuge operations, and informal access can differ materially.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'Wear a fitted PFD and carry a communication plan, spare paddle, light, food, and a cold-water layer. Keep the group together in the marked channel and stay visible to powerboats, fishing traffic, and bridges.',
      'Use USGS 04237496 as broad proxy context only. The official section source publishes no numeric runnable band; inspect actual canal level, wind, debris, vegetation, weather, and every access before launch.',
      'Treat Lock E26 as a portage/navigation control. Stay outside its warning buoys and movable-dam cable; never enter the dam-control area or assume the hand launch authorizes passage through the lock.',
      'When the Clyde meets or leaves the canal, follow the green and red canal buoys for the navigation channel. Unmarked river loops can be clogged with vegetation and debris, and the route boundary ends at Armitage before the refuge corridor.',
    ],
    shuttle: 'Stage the downstream vehicle only after confirming the informal Armitage Road bank access, then drive to Lyons Dock/Southside Canal Park or Lauraville Landing. Allow substantial time for a long marsh shuttle, free-permit camping coordination, Lock E26 carries, vegetation, remote extraction, and a conservative daylight margin.',
    camping: 'Lauraville Landing/Village of Clyde allows camping with a free permit obtained from the village office during business hours. Treat that as a managed, access-point camping option rather than dispersed bank camping; confirm current permit, space, vehicle, fire, and seasonal rules directly. No camping is claimed at Armitage, Lock E26, the canal bank, or the Montezuma refuge.',
    campingClassification: 'endpoint_campground',
    permits: 'Obtain the free Lauraville camping permit if staying there. Confirm current Canal Corporation lock and bridge procedures, Lyons/Clyde dock rules, Armitage access permission, parking, refuge boundaries, boating/PFD requirements, and any seasonal closure or event notices before departure.',
    accessCaveats: [
      'The stored coordinates follow official Canalway guide and public access-area anchors; dock, ramp, bank, parking, carry, lock, cable, bridge, camping, and refuge conditions remain subject to current local operation.',
      'Lauraville is the strongest documented intermediate public launch and managed camping location. Lock E26 is a hand-launch context but includes a movable-dam exclusion cable; confirm a legal carry and never enter the control area.',
      'The Armitage Road launch is explicitly informal. Verify legal unloading, parking, bank stability, landowner/refuge boundaries, and a usable take-out before starting a one-way trip.',
      'The route ends at Armitage Road before the Montezuma National Wildlife Refuge corridor. Continuing east requires a separate Section 14 route, refuge/access review, and new shuttle plan.',
    ],
