    summary: 'An 11.7-mile one-way Erie Canal Water Trail section from the Armitage/County Line boundary through the Montezuma National Wildlife Refuge wetland complex to the Town of Mentz Boat Ramp. The official stewardship inventory identifies this as Section 14 with upper and lower Mays Point access, an informal Richmond Aqueduct pull-out, Howland Island WMA, and Town of Mentz. The guidebook documents Lock E25 and its Mays Point launch contexts, the Richmond Aqueduct wood-debris warning, refuge and channel-divergence navigation, Howland Island’s difficult road approach, Montezuma Anchorage paddle camping, and the Mentz ramp’s 24-hour overnight-parking limit.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only marsh and canal route. Launch at a confirmed Armitage, Mays Point, or other legal water entry, portage or stop at Lock E25, follow canal buoys at Richmond/Hog/Haiti Island channel splits, treat Howland Island as a difficult-to-reach DEC landing, and finish at the Town of Mentz ramp before the Section 15 Seneca River corridor.',
