    summary: 'A 6.1-mile one-way Erie Canal Water Trail transition around Sylvan Beach and Verona Beach, from the Oneida Lake breakwater through the east-shore canal corridor toward Lock E21/New London. The official stewardship inventory identifies this as Section 18 with Verona Beach Car Top Launch, Squires Landing, the Sylvan Beach hand-launch context, and Cove Road Boat Launch. The guidebook documents the deceptive breakwater, busy summer resort traffic, side-channel landing, Lock E22 lift, Wood Creek debris, Verona Beach State Park camping, and the Lock E21 boundary.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only lake-edge and canal transition. Launch from a confirmed Verona Beach, Squires Landing, or Cove Road access, stay south of marker R106 at the breakwater, avoid private marina facilities, treat Oneida Lake weather and boat traffic as decisive, portage or stop at Lock E22 as required, and finish before Lock E21 unless a separate downstream route plan is in place.',
