    summary: 'A 5.5-mile one-way tidal Nissequogue River route from Paul T. Given County Park in Smithtown to the Nissequogue River State Park launch in Kings Park, with a conditional Sunken Meadow State Park mouth access. Suffolk County describes the 5.5-mile paddle, NYSDEC lists the public launch coordinates and kayak/canoe restrictions, and NYS Parks documents the tide-dependent launch window and mud-flat limitation. The route is planning-only: tide, wind, shallow water, park access, bridges, marsh channels, and the choice to reverse direction can matter more than the historical USGS record.',
