    shuttle: 'For a one-way trip, stage the downstream vehicle at confirmed Nissequogue River State Park, then drive to Paul T. Given County Park. Reconfirm tide direction and both park access windows immediately before launch; retain a turnaround plan if the tide, wind, depth, or landing does not match the plan.',
    camping: 'No on-route camping is claimed. Nissequogue River State Park and Sunken Meadow are day-use launch contexts; arrange separate lodging or a currently open managed campground and do not camp at the river banks, marsh islands, launch docks, or park facilities without explicit authorization.',
    campingClassification: 'nearby_basecamp',
    permits: 'Confirm current Suffolk County and NYS Parks launch, parking, vehicle-fee, park-hours, tide-window, kayak/canoe-only, marina, fishing, swimming, and seasonal rules. Check Long Island Sound marine advisories and comply with New York clean-drain-dry requirements before departure.',
    accessCaveats: [
      'The stored coordinates follow current NYSDEC public-launch records. They identify the launch area, not a guarantee that the dock, beach, carry, parking, or park access is open at the planned tide.',
      'Paul T. Given and Nissequogue River State Park are public hand launches; Sunken Meadow is retained as a conditional mouth-area access because the state directory separately lists the Nissequogue/Long Island Sound Field 3 launch.',
      'Nissequogue River State Park launching and returning are explicitly tide dependent, and the state guide warns of mud flats at low tide. Do not force the boat through exposed mud or use an unlisted bank as a substitute landing.',
      'The route ends at Nissequogue River State Park before the Long Island Sound mouth. Continuing into the Sound, using a different park field, or entering upstream freshwater requires separate current, access, and marine-safety planning.',
    ],
