    difficultyNotes: 'American Whitewater rates the broader section Class II–III and identifies 40–50-foot Harper Falls as a mandatory carry, plus Class III ledges, wavetrains, shallow landings, and early-runoff wood risk. Seasonal conservation-easement access, remote rescue, cold water, and limited exit options make the route advanced despite its mostly moderate rapids.',
