    summary: 'An advanced planning-only 22.1-mile South Branch Moose River reach from the public Rock Dam Road/Trail access near the Red River confluence to the McKeever bridge take-out. American Whitewater publishes the Class II–IV reach, route geometry, endpoint access points, ALC traverse boundary, 2.65-ft McKeever gauge condition, and portage context. NYSDEC documents the public Rock Dam Road end-of-road parking and the seasonal gate/road system; the ALC section is private land governed by navigation-only rules, with no camping, fishing, bank entry, or overnighting inside the traverse.',
    statusText: 'Advanced planning-only whitewater. Register and follow the ALC traverse terms, launch only from the confirmed Rock Dam access, carry or scout where required, remain on the water except strictly incidental navigation, and complete the private-land section in daylight before camping outside it. The 2.65-ft McKeever reading is a minimum access condition, not a go signal; wood, rapid hydraulics, cold water, weather, road gates, and the group’s rescue margin control the trip.',
