    shuttle: 'Stage the McKeever downstream vehicle only at the confirmed public take-out/parking context, then drive to the Rock Dam Road end through the seasonal Moose River Plains gate system. Confirm both gates, road drying, registration, daylight, and a failed-shuttle/extraction plan; a single vehicle is not an adequate rescue plan for this remote reach.',
    camping: 'NYSDEC documents numerous legal primitive roadside campsites in the Moose River Plains Complex, including along Rock Dam Road, but the ALC traverse prohibits camping and all non-navigation activity. Camp only at a separately confirmed DEC site outside the private section, and plan to complete the traverse before dusk; no riverbank, bridge, or private-land camping is claimed.',
    campingClassification: 'nearby_basecamp',
    permits: 'Follow the current ALC navigation terms and registration statement, NYSDEC Moose River Plains gate/road and camping rules, New York boating/PFD requirements, and any seasonal closures. The ALC terms provide no safety warranty and do not authorize camping, fishing, hunting, swimming, or general bank access.',
    accessCaveats: [
      'Rock Dam Road is a seasonal DEC access road; the UMP says it can remain closed after the area initially opens until it dries, and the route source identifies public access down DEC dirt roads. Verify the current gate and road status before carrying in.',
      'The ALC section is private property crossed under a narrow navigation settlement/order. Register, respect the specified season and gauge condition, stay on the water except incidental navigation, and do not infer a general public shoreline or camping right from navigability.',
      'The McKeever point is an American Whitewater route-source take-out anchor near the Route 28 bridge, not a surveyed ramp. Confirm the current river-right landing, parking, traffic exposure, and safe carry before launch.',
    ],
