    summary: 'A planning-only 23-mile tidal Hudson River water-trail corridor from the public Schodack Island State Park launch to the public Dutchman’s Landing launch at the mouth of Catskill Creek. NYSDEC and the Hudson River Greenway Water Trail identify the endpoint access chain and intervening estuary, while the direct Catskill USGS station provides local stage context. This is an exposed working-river crossing with no invented cfs go/no-go rule; tide, wind, waves, wakes, commercial traffic, cold water, and current water-quality information control the decision.',
