    difficultyNotes: 'American Whitewater rates the reach Class I–III(IV): the first mile is moving Class I–II, then the river builds to continuous Class II–III with a few more challenging drops. Wood, cold water, limited bailout options, and the lower-section boundary require confident boat control and conservative scouting.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High corridor and gauge confidence with access-anchor caveats: American Whitewater publishes the matching 5.7-mile upper reach, named Bailey Road put-in, Donnattsburg Road take-out, Class I–III(IV) character, and direct gauge association. DEC confirms public road access in the Bailey corridor and USGS provides the direct 04256000 station at Donnattsburg. The access coordinates are bridge/road anchors rather than surveyed ramps, so verify the legal carry and landing on site.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'Treat this as a serious whitewater run, not a casual float. Wear a fitted PFD and whitewater-appropriate protective gear, carry a throw bag and reliable communication, and paddle with a group whose skills match continuous Class II–III water and the harder drops.',
      'Use the American Whitewater route page and USGS 04256000 for same-day flow context, but never let a favorable number replace scouting. Low water can expose rocks and wood; rising water can remove eddies, increase holes, and turn a marginal feature into a swim or rescue problem.',
      'Scout the first mile, bridge approaches, continuous sections, blind bends, strainers, and any drop you cannot read from the boat. Portage or turn around before committing to a feature or losing the downstream exit margin.',
      'Use only the Bailey Road and Donnattsburg Road access contexts. Public road access does not grant blanket permission to park, cross private land, camp, or use an unposted bank; follow DEC rules and local signs.',
      'Donnattsburg is a hard boundary for this card. The lower Independence section is separately rated more difficult; do not continue downstream without a new route, access, safety, and rescue review.',
    ],
