    summary: 'An approximately 8.5-mile advanced whitewater planning route from the public NYSDEC hand launch below Lows Lower Dam to the public Bog River Falls Day Use Area on Tupper Lake. American Whitewater lists the connected reach as Round Lake Outlet—Round Lake to Bog River, Class IV–V, with four miles of flatwater, tight Class IV ledges, later IV+/V drops, and a Bog River Falls finale. NYSDEC independently confirms the public Lower Dam hand launch, spring-only lower rapids, three named canoe carries, and the public Bog River Falls entry. The route is bounded at Bog River Falls and does not claim a Round Lake launch or any dam descent.',
    statusText: 'Expert whitewater only and spring/high-water dependent. The American Whitewater 4.5–7 ft range is proxy context on Hudson River at North Creek, not a local clearance. Confirm current Lower Dam access, local water and trend, recent rain, trees, all three carries, weather, rescue plan, and the Bog River Falls landing; never run or approach the entry dam, and do not continue beyond the designated take-out into Tupper Lake without a separate plan.',
