    shuttle: 'Stage the downstream vehicle at the DEC Bog River Falls Day Use Area only after confirming current Route 421 access, parking, landing, and take-out conditions, then drive to the Lower Dam hand launch. Review the three carries, emergency exits, daylight, and a no-go turnaround before launching.',
    camping: 'NYSDEC documents designated campsites in the Bog River Complex, including sites in the connected Tupper Lake/Horseshoe Lake context, but does not establish a campsite on this whitewater reach. Use only currently designated/available sites or a separately verified nearby basecamp; no launch, dam, carry, day-use, or private-bank camping is claimed.',
    campingClassification: 'nearby_basecamp',
    permits: 'Follow current NYSDEC Bog River Complex and Forest Preserve rules, New York PFD/boating and invasive-species requirements, dam and carry restrictions, posted parking/day-use rules, designated-campsite limits, and private-property boundaries. Public water access does not authorize landing or camping everywhere along the route.',
    accessCaveats: [
      'The Lower Dam hand launch is a DEC-published water-entry anchor, but gates, road surface, parking, dam exclusion areas, carry surfaces, and the exact wetted-edge entry can change. Verify them in person before loading boats.',
      'The Bog River Falls Day Use Area is an official public entry context, not a guarantee of a whitewater take-out ramp. Walk the landing and identify a safe exit before launch; take out before the falls and do not use private shoreline as a backup.',
      'The AW listing is titled Round Lake Outlet—Round Lake to Bog River, while its endpoint and geometry begin at Lows Lower Dam. This card uses the DEC-confirmed Lower Dam start and retains the AW name as an alias; it does not claim a Round Lake launch.',
      'NYSDEC names three carries on the lower Bog River. Their current trail surfaces, portage lines, water levels, and private-shore boundaries require day-of confirmation; no intermediate carry coordinate is presented as an exact surveyed launch.',
    ],
