    summary: 'A roughly 14.5-mile wilderness canoe route from the public Bog River Flow hand launch at Lows Lower Dam through Hitchins Pond, around the short Lows Upper Dam carry, and across Lows Lake to the public western Lows Lake hand launch. NYSDEC documents the route, hand-launch coordinates, carry, wind-protected shoreline strategy, 39 numbered shoreline campsites, private-land cautions, loon habitat, and no-public-motorboat rule. This card stops at the western Lows Lake launch and does not imply the separate 3.5-mile Oswegatchie carry or the lower Bog River rapids.',
    statusText: 'This is a planning-only wilderness canoe route, not a simple flatwater loop. Launch at the DEC Lower Dam hand launch, carry around Lows Upper Dam, and keep a conservative shoreline route on Lows Lake; wind can create whitecaps quickly, and the northern shoreline is generally more protected. Confirm Lower Dam Road access, dam and carry conditions, weather, water temperature, private shoreline, campsite availability, and the return/shuttle plan before committing.',
