    summary: 'A planning-only approximately 5-mile lower Nine Mile Creek moving-water corridor from the creek-adjacent Munro Park practical put-in in the Village of Camillus to the documented Pumphouse Road / Honeywell Canoe and Kayak Launch area. The Nine Mile Creek Conservation Council identifies Munro Park as the highest practical lower-half put-in, NYSDEC confirms public creek access and a canoe/kayak launch in the watershed, and official DEC emergency-response material identifies the Pumphouse Road canoe/boat launch area. The historical Marietta USGS station is retained as a clearly labeled same-creek proxy only; it has no current data and supplies no runnable number.',
