    summary: 'A planning-only approximately 4.5-mile Raquette River whitewater reach from the current NYSDEC Forked Lake Campground and Day Use Area hand launch to the Deerland lean-to / Long Lake boundary. American Whitewater documents the Class II–III rock gardens, mandatory Buttermilk Falls portage, exact reach geometry, and the small Deerland access area; NYSDEC independently lists the Forked Lake launch, the Raquette River hand-launch corridor, North Point Road access to Buttermilk Falls, and the surrounding public wild-forest/camping setting. The Piercefield USGS station is a downstream same-river proxy, so local water, recent rain, wood, and a visual scout control the decision.',
