    summary: 'A planning-only approximately 5.5-mile Wallkill River segment from the NYSDEC-listed New Paltz hand launch to the NYSDEC-listed Rosendale hand launch. The Wallkill River Water Trail inventory identifies both access areas as active launches, and a documented New Paltz-to-Rosendale community paddle supports the distinct connection between the existing Gardiner-to-New Paltz card and the Sturgeon Pool boundary.',
    statusText: 'Use direct USGS 01371500 at Gardiner for route-context flow information. The Wallkill River Watershed Alliance says flows under 1,000 cfs may be too shallow, 1,000–2,000 cfs are generally navigable with some rapids, and flows above 2,000 cfs may be swift; these are planning bands, not a safety certification. Launch and take out only at the named public sites, inspect wood, shallow gravel, water quality, and current, and stop at Rosendale before the Sturgeon Pool dam/impoundment and any private or utility access.',
