    summary: 'A planning-only approximately 7-mile Rondout Creek out-and-back from the public T.R. Gallo Park cartop launch in Kingston to the Eddyville Dam boundary and back. The Hudson River Greenway identifies T.R. Gallo as a Rondout Creek cartop launch with waterfront services, while a Mid-Hudson Adirondack Mountain Club paddle documents the Kingston-waterfront-to-Eddyville-Dam line and return. The route stays on the lower creek, uses the Rosendale USGS station only as a same-creek proxy, and does not claim passage over the dam, private waterfront landing, or overnight access.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only slow-moving creek and tidal-transition loop. Launch from the T.R. Gallo Park water-trail site after confirming current city access, carry, parking, and waterfront activity; paddle upstream only to the Eddyville Dam boundary, then return to the same launch. Check the Rosendale proxy trend with tide/current, wind, local depth, debris, cold-water conditions, and the actual channel. Do not approach the dam, use private marinas or shipyards as landings, or infer a through-route from the public waterway.',
