    hazards: ['fast_rise', 'strainers', 'cold_water', 'private_banks', 'urban_water_quality', 'access_uncertain', 'mandatory_takeout'],
    difficulty: 'moderate',
    difficultyNotes: 'The upper pool is described as slow-moving and suitable for small boats, but the lower creek is tidal-transition water with current, wind, shipyard and tour-boat traffic, rail and bridge constraints, cold-water exposure, and a hard dam boundary. A return-to-launch objective requires reliable self-rescue and enough margin for the upstream leg and return.',
    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 01367500 at Rosendale is an active same-creek station upstream of the Kingston/Eddyville reach and reports live flow context, but reservoir conservation releases, the Eddyville dam, tide, wind, local depth, debris, and urban conditions can decouple its reading from this route. USGS 01372005 at Eddyville is a historical/no-current-data site and is used only as location context.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High bounded-corridor and launch-context confidence: the current Hudson River Greenway lists T.R. Gallo as a Rondout Creek cartop launch with tide information and services; NYSDEC lists a separate public Rondout Creek launch above Eddyville; and the Mid-Hudson Adirondack Mountain Club documents the Kingston-waterfront-to-Eddyville-Dam paddle and return. Gauge confidence is moderate as a clearly labeled upstream proxy, and the route remains planning-only because the local loop line, water depth, dam approach, and emergency landing options require same-day inspection.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'Wear a fitted PFD and carry a spare paddle, whistle, dry communication device, map, light, first-aid kit, water, and a clean-drain-dry kit. File an out-and-back float plan and keep enough daylight and energy for the return to T.R. Gallo.',
      'Use the Rosendale gauge as trend context only; no numeric runnable band is asserted. Check tide/current, wind, thunderstorms, water temperature, local depth, debris, wakes, and any water-quality advisory immediately before departure.',
      'Keep clear of the Eddyville Dam, hydraulic water, bridge and rail structures, working waterfront, tour boats, marinas, shipyards, and private banks. Do not land on a private shoreline or use a service road, marina, or fishing point as an improvised exit.',
      'Turn around early if the upstream leg, wind/current, channel depth, floating wood, traffic, weather, or daylight margin makes the return uncertain. The Gallo launch is the planned finish; do not continue into the Hudson, Wallkill, or upper Rondout without a separate route and access review.',
    ],
    shuttle: 'No shuttle is required. Stage at the confirmed T.R. Gallo Park cartop-launch area, carry to the creek, paddle upstream to the Eddyville boundary, and return to the same launch. Allow extra time for Kingston waterfront events, tour-boat traffic, parking, bridge/rail crossings, tide, and a conservative return window.',
