    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 01510000 at Cincinnatus is a direct Otselic River station with a long period of record and current stage/discharge telemetry. It is downstream of the Willet launch, so local rain, tributary timing, shallow reach effects, debris, and bridge hydraulics can differ materially; no universal runnable cutoff is asserted.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High endpoint confidence for the bounded section: current NYS Parks launch listings and the current Cortland County paddling page identify both named public hand launches and their coordinates. Gauge confidence is high for direct same-river trend context, while route mileage, local depth, wood, bridge conditions, and any unlisted emergency landing require same-day field verification.',
