    summary: 'A planning-only approximately 6-mile North Branch Saranac River out-and-back from the current NYSDEC hand launch near North Branch Road and Mountain Pond Road toward the Lake Kushaqua approach. DEC documents the non-motorized hand launch and warns that the river is fast-moving and not for beginners; the Kushaqua recreation plan and connected-waterway guidance document a scenic stream valley, occasional obstructions and beaver dams, and links through Kushaqua Narrows toward Lake Kushaqua and Buck Pond. The route returns to the hand launch; the lake approach is a water-only turnaround, not a vehicle take-out.',
    statusText: 'Launch only after confirming the DEC access path, dock, parking, road status, and river conditions. Paddle the North Branch toward the Lake Kushaqua approach, turn around before current, wood, shallow water, beaver activity, wind, private/easement boundaries, or daylight margin compromise the group, and return to the same hand launch. The downstream Plattsburgh gauge is a broad Saranac proxy only and supplies no local go/no-go cutoff.',
