    summary: 'An advanced planning-only approximately 17.5-mile high-water Grass River continuation from the current NYSDEC DeGrasse State Forest hand launch through the South Branch/main Grass River corridor to the public Pyrites Route 21 kayak/canoe launch. NYSDEC describes the South Branch as challenging whitewater used during high water and identifies falls and portage trails throughout the complex; DEC separately confirms the DeGrasse hand launch and river frontage, while a current NYS DPS access document identifies the Pyrites launch as public, ADA accessible, and served by safe roadside loading/unloading. The route ends at Pyrites before the hydropower-dam boundary and does not claim a downstream portage or continuation to Canton.',
    statusText: 'Advanced high-water planning route only. Confirm the DeGrasse launch, local water and recent rain, every required carry, wood, road access, and the Pyrites landing before committing. Portage all marked falls and unscouted drops, and take out at the Pyrites Route 21 launch before the hydropower dam; do not infer a safe dam portage or Canton continuation from the public launch.',
