    difficultyNotes: 'American Whitewater lists this reach from Class II to V+ depending on flow and describes a dam drop, Class III water, bedrock, wood, and branch-junction features. Treat it as hard whitewater requiring competent boaters, scouting, rescue training, cold-water protection, and a deliberate portage or withdrawal plan; the 1,000-cfs observation is not a safety rating.',
    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 04268800 is a live West Branch St. Regis River station near Parishville used by American Whitewater for this Middle Branch reach. It is a same-watershed proxy, not a local waterline: Middle Branch inflow, recent rain, release operations, wood, and the route’s bedrock features can diverge materially.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High corridor confidence: American Whitewater publishes the named Route 458-to-St. Regis Falls section, approximate 4.1-mile length, flow-dependent Class II–V+ range, feature hazards, and proxy gauge. High upstream access confidence: current NYSDEC Franklin County data lists the Santa Clara Flow/St. Regis River hard-surface launch and coordinates. Conditional finish confidence: the Town of Waverly confirms ownership and operation of the riverfront campsite, but paddlers must obtain current permission for the campground carry, landing, parking, and staging.',
    safetyNotes: [
      'This is advanced whitewater for experienced groups with fitted PFDs, helmets, cold-water protection, throw bags, rescue training, spare gear, communications, and a written extraction plan. Scout the actual line and recovery pool before committing.',
      'Use the approximate 1,000-cfs American Whitewater observation only as contextual flow guidance. The 04268800 West Branch proxy cannot certify Middle Branch conditions; inspect local stage, recent rain, dam operations, wood, hydraulics, and downstream recovery in person.',
      'Identify and portage the dam drop or any unrunnable feature from a lawful, pre-scouted route. Never approach a hydraulic, falls, bridge, intake, or private-bank landing because a map or gauge appears favorable.',
      'Finish at the Town of Waverly campsite only with current permission and a confirmed below-falls landing. Do not extend downstream into the separate Silver Staircase route, use Nicholville or road shoulders as an assumed bailout, or land on private shoreline.',
    ],
    shuttle: 'Stage the downstream vehicle at the St. Regis Falls Scenic Campsite only after obtaining current campground permission, then drive to the NYSDEC Santa Clara Flow launch. Allow time for the long shuttle, campground check-in, scouting, dam/wood decisions, and alternate extraction if the permission, waterline, or take-out fails.',
    camping: 'The Town of Waverly St. Regis Falls Scenic Campsite provides tent, RV, cabin, and lean-to options beside the river, but camping, overnight parking, and river access require current reservation or permission and compliance with campsite rules. No dispersed camping is claimed at the launch, dam, bridges, private banks, or intervening shoreline.',
    campingClassification: 'endpoint_campground',
    permits: 'Obtain current Town of Waverly campsite permission for the river finish, carry, parking, and camping; follow NYSDEC launch, Clean.Drain.Dry, boating/PFD, state-land, private-property, dam/operator, and posted whitewater rules. Public DEC launch status does not authorize the campground or any private-bank portage.',
    accessCaveats: [
      'NYSDEC currently lists Santa Clara Flow/St. Regis River as a public hard-surface launch, but seasonal access, gates, parking, shallow water, and carry conditions must be confirmed in the field.',
      'The Town of Waverly campsite is a managed municipal facility, not an unconditional public boat ramp. Call ahead, obtain permission, check in, and confirm the exact below-falls landing and vehicle staging before relying on it.',
      'The Route 458-to-St. Regis Falls route ends before the existing St. Regis Falls-to-Fort Jackson Silver Staircase card. Do not merge the two route records or use the downstream card’s conditional Fort Jackson access to justify this finish.',
    ],
