    summary: 'A planning-only approximately six-mile Sangerfield River out-and-back from the Town of Hamilton’s public 9-Mile Park on Wickwire Road into Nine Mile Swamp. The Town acquired the riverfront property to secure public recreational access, NYSDEC authorized a public kayak launch and parking improvements, and current local tourism material describes a gentle three-mile water reach suitable for kayaking and canoeing. The route returns to the confirmed launch rather than claiming a second roadside or private-bank take-out.',
    statusText: 'Planning-only flatwater/wetland route. Use the town launch and off-street parking at 9-Mile Park, paddle upstream into the Sangerfield/Nine Mile Swamp corridor only while the channel is visibly open and navigable, and turn around before wood, vegetation, darkness, heat, or fatigue removes a safe margin. The 01505000 Chenango gauge is a basin proxy, not a local threshold; no camping or private-bank landing is implied.',
