    gaugeStatusNote: 'USGS 01505000 is a live Chenango River station near Sherburne, downstream and on the receiving river rather than the Sangerfield reach. It provides broad basin rainfall and flow trend context only; local Sangerfield/Nine Mile Swamp water depth, vegetation, wood, and access conditions can diverge materially.',
    confidenceNotes: 'High public-access confidence: the Town of Hamilton identifies the 9-Mile Park river access and kayak launch, and NYSDEC’s completed permit authorizes a public kayak launch and parking improvements at the Sangerfield River site. Moderate route-distance and exact-water-entry confidence: current local material describes roughly three miles each way into Nine Mile Swamp, while the coordinate is an approximate geocoded address-to-water-entry anchor. The route remains planning-only because the gauge is a receiving-river proxy and no numeric local paddling cutoff is published.',
