      'The Sangerfield/Nine Mile Swamp corridor can be warm, still, buggy, and difficult to exit. Paddle with daylight and a reserve, keep the group together, and do not continue beyond the approximately three-mile turnaround when navigation, water depth, vegetation, or fatigue is deteriorating.',
      'Stay on the water or use only the public launch area. Do not land, scout, camp, or portage across private shoreline, farm fields, wetland vegetation, road shoulders, or unmarked banks, and follow current Town, DEC, wildlife, and water-quality notices.',
