      'Treat the Buffalo River confluence as a hard route boundary. Motorized traffic, wakes, wind, and the open river can change the hazard profile immediately beyond the park egress.',
      'Use daylight and a conservative alternate extraction plan; the urban corridor has limited room for an improvised carry if the creek is blocked.',
